    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, returning **400**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`BuildOwner.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 where the owner's registration date is read before defaulting/business-day rollover, added a guard: if a date was *supplied* (non-null) and it `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, throw the new checked exception. An absent date still defaults to the server date, and a date on/before today is accepted as before.\n\n2. **`RegistrationDateInFutureException.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 new checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`RegistrationDateInFutureExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 maps the exception to a `400 BAD_REQUEST` `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **`officefloor/escalation/\u2026RegistrationDateInFutureException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\nThe `PUT /owners/{ownerId}` path doesn't touch `registrationDate`, so creation is the only affected endpoint. The acceptance test (`errorRejectsFutureDate`, posting `2999-01-01`) passes and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
